padya", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vedic-index-macdonell-keith", "senses": [{"gloss": "Vaiyāghra-padya, ‘descendant of Vyāghrapad,’ is the patronymic of Indradyumna bhāllaveya in the Śatapatha brāhmaṇa and the Chāndogya upaniṣad, of buḍila āśvatarāśvi in the Chāndogya upaniṣad, and of Gośruti in that upaniṣad and in the śāṅkhāyana Āraṇyaka. In the Jaiminīya upaniṣad brāhmaṇa the patronymic is applied to rāma krātujāteya.\nFoot notes x. 6, 1, 8.\nv. 14, 1.\nv. 16, 1.\nv. 2, 3.\nix. 7 (Gośruta-vaiyāghrapadya as a compound).\niii. 40, 1; iv. 16. 1.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["padya", "vaiyaaghra", "vaiyaaghra-padya", "vaiyaaghrapadya", "vaiyāghra", "vaiyāghra-padya", "vaiyāghrapadya", "पद्य", "वैयाघ्र", "वैयाघ्रपद्य", "పద్య", "వైయాఘ్ర", "వైయాఘ్ర-పద్య", "వైయాఘ్రపద్య", "ಪದ್ಯ", "ವೈಯಾಘ್ರ", "ವೈಯಾಘ್ರ-ಪದ್ಯ", "ವೈಯಾಘ್ರಪದ್ಯ"], "synonyms_slp1": ["padya", "vaiyaaghra", "vaiyaaghra-padya", "vaiyaaghrapadya", "vaiyāghra", "vaiyāghra-padya", "vaiyāghrapadya", "padya", "vEyAGra", "vEyAGrapadya", "పద్య", "వైయాఘ్ర", "వైయాఘ్ర-పద్య", "వైయాఘ్రపద్య", "ಪದ್ಯ", "ವೈಯಾಘ್ರ", "ವೈಯಾಘ್ರ-ಪದ್ಯ", "ವೈಯಾಘ್ರಪದ್ಯ"]}], "vEyaska": [{"id": "vEyAska", "headword": "वैयास्क", "headword_slp1": "vEyAska", "fold": "vEyaska", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vedic-index-macdonell-keith", "senses": [{"gloss": "Vaiyāska is read in one passage of the Rigveda Prātiśākhya, as the name of an authority on the metres of the Rigveda. Roth is clearly right in thinking that yāska is meant.\nFoot notes xvii. 25.\nSt. Petersburg Dictionary, s.v.\nThe name not being a patronymic from Viyāska, but standing for vai Yāskaḥ, Cf. vaijāna.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["vaiyaaska", "vaiyāska", "వైయాస్క", "ವೈಯಾಸ್ಕ"], "synonyms_slp1": ["vaiyaaska", "vaiyāska", "వైయాస్క", "ವೈಯಾಸ್ಕ"]}]}